{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"A persistent host firewall is enabled on node1 and recovers after restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Firewalld was active and enabled before restart. The acknowledged restart changed the boot ID, after which firewalld was again active and enabled with matching runtime and permanent policy. The fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-432045500dc447ec","cmd-742b9fd122174e15","cmd-3a52703fcc684f9d","cmd-543cc4b167444f87","cmd-9208212e2a184311","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The firewall permits inbound SSH and TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both runtime and permanent public-zone configurations allow SSH and 8080/tcp. Active nftables rules explicitly accept TCP destination ports 22 and 8080, including after restart; SSH also recovered with IPv4 and IPv6 listeners.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3b0c74f291324fb3","cmd-abd0eefb548b4d37","cmd-9208212e2a184311","cmd-ccba95245b0e4656"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Unrelated inbound connections are rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active public zone has a REJECT target and contains only the requested SSH service and 8080/tcp port. The generated nftables input path accepts those ports and ends unmatched inbound processing with an administrative reject, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3b0c74f291324fb3","cmd-abd0eefb548b4d37","cmd-c337e051474f4d58","cmd-9208212e2a184311","cmd-ccba95245b0e4656"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The permanent firewalld changes directly established the required policy, and the transient scheduled reboot served the mandatory restart protocol and disappeared through that restart. Final observations show no failed services, package damage, or unexplained residue; temporary-file and socket differences are normal restart-related identity/PID changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d15d849dd13c4842","cmd-742b9fd122174e15","cmd-ccba95245b0e4656","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 has an enabled, persistent firewalld policy that allows SSH and TCP 8080, rejects other new inbound traffic, and recovered coherently after a verified reboot. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for the sole managed node and agrees with the fixed lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":["No external packet-level connection tests were captured; allow/reject behavior is established from the active generated nftables rules and firewalld state.","No service was listening on TCP 8080, so application reachability on that port was not demonstrated; the task required the firewall allowance, which was directly observed."]}
